<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-CSR year net falls to A$212.2 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-CSR year net falls to A$212.2 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    322.0 vs 487.7</p>
<p>    Net				     212.2 vs 330.8</p>
<p>    Final dividend (cents)		9.0 vs 15.0</p>
<p>NOTE: CSR Ltd is a building products manufacturer and sugar refiner.  </p>
<p>    Profit pre interest and tax    461.80 vs 619.80</p>
<p>    Total dividend (cents)	    21.00 vs 29.00</p>
<p>    Sales (billion)			6.13 vs 6.14</p>
<p>    Other income			 311.90 vs 236.20</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			   21.60 vs 34.70</p>
<p>    Abnormal items			  nil vs gain 7.40</p>
<p>Dividend is 50 percent franked</p>
<p>Pay date July 2</p>
<p>Reg date June 4</p>
<p>    Tax				     95.90 vs 136.50</p>
<p>    Interest			     164.60 vs 153.90</p>
<p>    Depreciation			 338.50 vs 311.80</p>
<p>NOTE: Divisional earnings after tax and minorities but before abnormals.</p>
<p>    Construction materials	    53.70 vs 62.80</p>
<p>    Building materials-Australia    31.20 vs 73.40</p>
<p>    CSR America			  117.70 vs 110.60</p>
<p>    Aluminium			     58.30 vs 77.60</p>
<p>    Timber				   4.10 vs 25.20</p>
<p>    Sugar				   53.60 vs 64.70</p>
<p>    Unallocated		    loss 18.20 vs loss 12.70</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 373 1800</p>
</text>
